.he "times (2)                    10/3/26                    times (2)"
.fo "				    -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
times
- get process times


.in -5
.bd
C
.in +5
.br
times(buffer)
.br
struct tms *buffer;


.in -5
.bd
FUNCTION
.in +5
.br
.bd
Times
fills the structure pointed to by buffer with the
CPU-time accounting of the current process and its
children.  The structure is:

.nf
struct tms
	{
	long	tms_utime,	/* user time */
		tms_stime;	/* system time */
	long	tms_cutime,	/* user time of children */
		tms_cstime;	/* system time of children */
	};
.fi

The children times are the sum of the children's process
times and their children's times.  The unit is the clock
tick: HERTZ per second on the kernel, Z80 cycles on the
simulator.


.in -5
.bd
RETURNS
.in +5
.br
A 0 indicates success, a -1 indicates failure.


.in -5
.bd
ASSEMBLER
.in +5
.br
.bd
(times = 43)
.br
.bd
times; buffer


.in -5
.bd
RETURNS
.in +5
.br
The carry flag is cleared on success, or set on failure.
On success the four longs are placed in the area
pointed at by buffer.
